{#
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    THE EDUS WORDMARK — the brand, and the only one.

    "Edus" is four letters. It does not need a glyph beside it to be recognised,
    and a mark + wordmark saying the same thing twice is a logo plus a caption
    arguing for the same space. So the word IS the logo:

        Edus.

    Serif, bold, tight tracking, closed with an accent full stop. The full stop
    is the one ornament, it is a single ink, and it therefore survives being
    printed in black and white, photocopied, or set in DejaVu Serif inside a PDF.

    ⚠️ Import this file and call the macro. Do not retype "Edus" by hand and do
    not reintroduce `images/brand/edus-mark.svg` — the mark was retired when the
    wordmark became the logo. The only mark left is the favicon
    (`edus-favicon.svg`), because a 16 px tab cannot hold a word.

    Usage:
        {% import '_brand.html.twig' as brand %}
        {{ brand.wordmark('md') }}            {# ink on a light background #}
        {{ brand.wordmark('lg', 'light') }}   {# white on a dark background #}
        {{ brand.lockup('dark') }}            {# wordmark + tagline #}
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#}

{#
    `size`: xs · sm · md · lg · xl
    `tone`: 'dark'  — ink on a light background (the default)
            'light' — white on a dark background
#}
{% macro wordmark(size = 'md', tone = 'dark') %}
    {%- set scale = {
        xs: 'text-sm',
        sm: 'text-lg',
        md: 'text-xl',
        lg: 'text-2xl',
        xl: 'text-4xl',
    } -%}
    {%- set colour = tone == 'light' ? 'text-white' : 'text-ink-900' -%}
    {%- set dot = tone == 'light' ? 'text-accent-400' : 'text-accent-600' -%}
    <span class="font-serif font-bold leading-none tracking-tight {{ scale[size]|default(scale.md) }} {{ colour }}">Edus<span class="{{ dot }}">.</span></span>
{%- endmacro %}

{#
    The wordmark plus the one-line descriptor. Used where the brand stands
    alone — the app footer, a standalone public page — never in a header that
    already names the school.
#}
{% macro lockup(tone = 'dark', size = 'sm') %}
    <span class="inline-flex flex-col leading-tight">
        {{ _self.wordmark(size, tone) }}
        <span class="mt-1.5 text-xs {{ tone == 'light' ? 'text-ink-300' : 'text-ink-500' }}">The school operating system</span>
    </span>
{%- endmacro %}
